# vocal-ai — Code Owners
#
# This file declares default and per-path ownership. GitHub uses it to auto-request
# reviews. The agent SDLC uses it to know who to ping when a change touches an
# area outside the current session's scope.
#
# Syntax: <pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Patterns follow .gitignore syntax. Owners can be GitHub usernames (@user) or
# team slugs (@org/team). Later matches win.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners/

# ── Default owner (applies to all files unless overridden below) ─────────────
# Shivam Mishra
*    @shmmsra

# ── Per-path overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add specific ownership rules as the project grows. Examples:
#
# Documentation owned by a docs lead:
# /docs/         @shmmsra
#
# CI / build infra owned by infra team:
# /.github/      @shmmsra
# /Makefile      @shmmsra
#
# Agent-config layer must be reviewed by anyone touching agent workflows:
# /CLAUDE.md     @shmmsra
# /AGENTS.md     @shmmsra
# /docs/agents/  @shmmsra
#
# Architecture decisions need an architect's sign-off:
# /docs/decisions/  @shmmsra
